# Project-wide rules
---
description: Global coding standards for the Astro project
globs: ["*"]
rules:
  - Each file must start with its path as a single-line comment
  - Comments should explain why, not what the code does
  - Follow DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principles
  - Optimize for performance and reusability
  - Maintain clear separation of concerns
---

# Astro Component Rules
---
description: Standards for Astro components and styling
globs: ["*.astro"]
rules:
  - Use TailwindCSS utility classes for all styling
  - Avoid inline styles
  - Keep components modular and reusable
  - Group related Tailwind utilities together
  - Extract common utility patterns into reusable components
---

# TypeScript Rules
---
description: TypeScript configuration and type safety
globs: ["*.tsx"]
rules:
  - Enable strict TypeScript mode
  - Explicitly declare all types
  - Avoid using 'any' type
  - Use proper type annotations for props and state
  - Implement proper error handling with type checking
---

# Component Structure
---
description: Component organization and best practices
globs: ["*.astro", "*.tsx"]
rules:
  - Components should have a single responsibility
  - Props should be properly typed
  - Maintain consistent naming conventions
  - Keep components focused and concise
  - Document component interfaces and usage
---